(2) KP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) has the duties to: a. formulate various comprehensive protection efforts for victims of violence;
b. raise awareness among women and children, especially victims of violence, regarding the importance of fulfilling human rights, based on institutions and community;
c. provide information and develop cooperation networks necessary in seeking protection for victims of violence; d. assist in empowering victims of violence in their capacity as family members and as members of society;
e. facilitate the availability of supporting facilities and infrastructure for the optimization of protection for victims of violence;
f. implement protection for women and children victims of violence. g. mobilize funding sources for the benefit of implementing protection for victims of violence.
h. carry out protection activities for victims of violence. i. provide services and protection to victims of violence. (3) KP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) reports the implementation of its duties to the Regent.
(4) Each division as referred to in paragraph (1) may be assisted by members according to needs.
(5) The membership of KP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of elements from: a. Regional Apparatus;
b. Professional Organizations;
c. Community Leaders;
d. Educational Institutions;
