translated_text:
Article 10
(1) Forms of violence against women and children include:
a. Physical violence;
b. Sexual violence;
c. Economic violence;
d. Psychological violence.
(2) Forms of physical violence as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a are any act that results in pain, injury, wounds or disability to a person's body, miscarriage, unconsciousness and or causes death.
(3) Forms of sexual violence as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b, are sexual harassment, forced sexual intercourse, forced sexual intercourse in an unnatural or unwanted manner, forced sexual intercourse with others for commercial purposes and or certain purposes.
(4) Forms of economic violence as referred to in paragraph (1) letter c are neglect of family members in the form of not providing a proper living, care or maintenance.
(5) Forms of psychological violence as referred to in paragraph (1) letter d are acts that result in fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and or severe psychological suffering in a person.
